So the problem is that this directory has its permissions clamped down pretty tight. You have it only readable/writable by root. Shiny Server doesn't run apps as root, as that would be a huge security risk, but instead by default runs as the "shiny" user. This user needs at least read and execute permissions on the app directory (and any subdirectories), and read permissions on any files therein.

These commands should do it (run them as root):

chown root:shiny /srv/shiny-server/election_project
chmod 750 /srv/shiny-server/election_project
chmod 640 /srv/shiny-server/election_project/*

