SockJS (the library we use for websocket emulation) has a variety of transports. It's possible the one it's choosing is not interacting well with your corporate firewall/proxy (for example, buffering responses from the server for 60 seconds). Try pressing Ctrl+Alt+Shift+A in IE9 when an app is loaded. Try unchecking the protocols one by one (hitting reload each time). In particular, unchecking the ones named *-streaming may do the trick.

