HI Rohan,

Apologies for the late response.

Yes, I was able to solve the issue.

My mistake was to thought that the issue was with the way I was using rdrop2.

Nonetheless, the issue really was the way I was using shiny.

In my code I included a reactive() function when I needed an observe().

reactive({

drop_get(paste("/Shiny_DB_Test/", filePutReport(), sep = ""),

dtoken = token)

That was my main problem.

Joe Cheng provides a very well explanation on the difference here:

https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/shiny-developer-conference/
If you continue having the problem, please, e-mail me again.
José

